schurComplex -- Schur functors of chain complexes
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G=schurComplex(lambda,F)
  * Inputs:
      * lambda, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * F, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 

Description
===========

This function computes the Schur complex associated to a partition $\lambda$
and a bounded complex $F_{\bullet}$ of finitely-generated free modules over a
commutative ring.

The user inputs the partition $\lambda$ as a list and the chain complex
$F_{\bullet}$.

In the following example, the complex F is the free resolution of the ideal
$(x,y,z)\subset \mathbb{Z}[x,y,z]$, and lambda is the partition $(1,1)$ in the
form of a List. In this case, the Schur complex G is the second exterior power
of F.



